        "original_id": "4fe8caa1-e9f7-5411-ac46-d9d573832ecb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Giacomo Meyerbeer, Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart\n- Works: L'esule di Granata\n- Roles: opera composer, composer\n- Concepts: nineteenth-century stage composition, Classical era, melodramma serio\n\nFacts:\n- Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart was born on 27 January 1756, was baptised as Johannes Chrysostomus Wolfgangus Theophilus Mozart, and was a prolific and influential composer of the Classical era.\n- Giacomo Meyerbeer was born as Jacob Liebmann Beer on 5 September 1791 and was a German opera composer of Jewish birth.\n- Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart died on 5 December 1791.\n- Giacomo Meyerbeer has been described as perhaps the most successful stage composer of the nineteenth century.\n- L'esule di Granata is a two-act melodramma serio by Giacomo Meyerbeer.\n- Giacomo Meyerbeer died on 2 May 1864.",
